\v 6 Ahishar¦158205 was¦158206 in charge of¦158210 the¦158215 palace¦158208,
\q1 and¦158209 Avda's¦158212 son¦158210 Adoniram¦158209 \add ≈supervised\add* the¦158210 forced¦158215 labourers¦158215.
\p
\v 7 Shelomoh¦158218 \add ≈appointed twelve governors¦158222\add* over¦158223 all¦158225 Yisrael¦158227, and¦158218 they¦158228 \add sent in\add* food for the palace¦158234—each¦158225 \add governor\add* was¦158237 responsible for one month¦158235 of¦158225 the year¦158236.
\v 8 Their¦158246 names¦158246 were¦158246:
\q1 Ben-Hur¦158249 in¦158250 the¦158250 hill¦158250 country¦158250 of¦158250 Efrayim¦158251,
\q1
\v 9 Ben¦158254-Deker¦158256 in¦158257 Makats¦158257, Shaalvim¦158258, Beyt-Shemesh, and¦158258 Eylon-Beyt¦158259-Hanan¦158263,
\q1
